WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.405
Step 1. Open the store location.

1.2
00:00:02.405 --> 00:00:07.524
In Care 3.1, you add a product when you receive a new batch from a supplier.

1.3
00:00:07.524 --> 00:00:12.788
Select Services, open the service, and select the store location.

2.1
00:00:12.788 --> 00:00:15.349
Step 2. Open Purchase Deliveries.

2.2
00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:19.620
In the location sidebar, under Inventory and External Supply,

2.3
00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:25.162
select Purchase Deliveries. Care shows the Inward Purchase Entries page.

3.1
00:00:25.162 --> 00:00:27.897
Step 3. Open the purchase delivery.

3.2
00:00:27.897 --> 00:00:32.370
In the Created tab, select View Details for the Draft delivery.

3.3
00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.781
You can add items only while it is Draft.

4.1
00:00:35.781 --> 00:00:43.279
Step 4. Add an item. Select Add Item. Care opens the Product picker of the new row.

5.1
00:00:43.279 --> 00:00:46.005
Step 5. Select the Product Knowledge.

5.2
00:00:46.005 --> 00:00:49.419
If your facility already has an Active batch of it,

5.3
00:00:49.419 --> 00:00:52.864
Care fills the row from the most recent one.

6.1
00:00:52.864 --> 00:00:55.571
Step 6. Enter the new batch number.

6.2
00:00:55.571 --> 00:01:00.415
Replace the earlier number with the new one, and select Create batch.

6.3
00:01:00.415 --> 00:01:04.355
The row shows New, so Care creates a new product.

7.1
00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:10.668
Step 7. Enter the batch details. Check the expiry, the category, and the pack size.

7.2
00:01:10.668 --> 00:01:16.574
Then enter the pack quantity, and the TPR, the purchase price of one pack.

8.1
00:01:16.574 --> 00:01:19.932
Step 8. Save the item. Select Save Changes.

8.2
00:01:19.932 --> 00:01:24.775
Care creates the product and lists the item under Items to Receive.

8.3
00:01:24.775 --> 00:01:28.384
The stock rises when you receive the items.
